2401","position":{"commit_sha":"3c55c31f78f9146286af9d873e19035341e029af","position":"1788457512454462001-a1213eae-1ec2-4276-a730-d1d0bee92401"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Removed the no-op caller-selected reviewer input from the three public review-code entry points: the CLI parser/handler no longer accepts or forwards --reviewer, the MCP review_code tool no longer advertises a reviewers parameter, and rebar.llm.review_code() now rejects reviewers= at the Python signature. Kept the output review_result reviewers field, regenerated the CLI/MCP reference artifacts and MCP/library parity manifest, corrected ADR 0075 and changelog wording, and added focused guards for parser rejection, no-forwarding, signature rejection, and reviewers-output preservation. Focused review-code tests, lint, typecheck, cli-help/reference checks, api-surface, and MCP/library parity are green. The default broad selector still carries a pre-existing atomic-close lifecycle baseline: the already-approved test_relevant_remote_rejection_never_places_candidate_on_shared_head plus four sibling failures in the same file that reproduce unchanged on a clean origin/main snapshot.","timestamp":1788441206683174001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788313649310830001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"4ad217ff-abc3-4225-9f14-27fa70082f80","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9199-1dc8-c0a4-4484"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe CLI and MCP still accepted caller-selected reviewer input at `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/llm.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py`, and `src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py`, while `src/rebar/llm/code_review/shim.py` ignored it and let the four-pass code-review gate select overlays internally. Callers could believe they chose reviewers even though the gate owned that decision.\n\n## Approach\n\nRemove reviewer-selection input from the CLI parser, CLI dispatch, MCP method/schema, and the keyword-only Python signature. Keep gate-owned overlay selection and the output `reviewers` field that reports which reviewers actually ran. Treat this as an intentional pre-1.0 breaking change with no deprecation shim.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/llm.py` and `src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py` remove CLI `--reviewer` parsing/forwarding and refresh generated help\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py`, `src/rebar/llm/code_review/shim.py`, and `src/rebar/llm/code_review/__init__.py` remove the MCP/library compatibility-only input and document the gate-backed surface accurately\n- `src/rebar/_cli/help/review-code.txt`, `docs/cli-reference.md`, `docs/mcp-reference.md`, `docs/adr/0075-retire-single-pass-code-review.md`, and `CHANGELOG.md` restate the new contract\n- `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_review_ops_characterization.py`, `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_cli_help_writing_guidelines_jerboa.py`, `tests/unit/test_advanced_cli_parsers.py`, `tests/unit/test_code_review_gate_session.py`, `tests/unit/test_code_review_provenance_heldout_2d1c.py`, `tests/unit/mcp_library_parity_manifest.json`, `tests/external/test_pydantic_ai_cutover_live.py`, and `tests/external/test_llm_trace.py` pin the input removal while preserving output reviewers reporting\n\nCascade flag: true. Recensus CLI, MCP, library, generated-doc, and test-fixture callers.\n\n## Testing\n\nExercise CLI parse failure on the removed flag, absence of forwarded `reviewers` kwargs, Python signature rejection, output `reviewers` preservation, CLI/help drift checks, MCP/library parity, and the default `make test` selector with only the known baseline lifecycle failure accepted.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] CLI `--reviewer`, MCP `review_code.reviewers`, and Python `reviewers=` inputs are absent from their contracts.\n- [x] Old calls fail at parsing, schema, or signature validation before a billable model call.\n- [x] Gate-owned reviewer selection remains and result `reviewers` accurately reports reviewers that ran.\n- [x] Docs, generated help/reference, and parity baselines state the pre-1.0 breaking replacement: omit selection and inspect result reviewers.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/llm.py","reason":"remove CLI --reviewer parsing from review-code"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py","reason":"stop forwarding caller-selected reviewers from the CLI handler"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py","reason":"remove the MCP review_code reviewers input"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/code_review/shim.py","reason":"drop the compatibility-only reviewers keyword from the library surface"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/code_review/__init__.py","reason":"document the gate-backed review_code surface without the old signature claim"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/review-code.txt","reason":"regenerated review-code help after removing --reviewer"},{"path":"docs/cli-reference.md","reason":"regenerated CLI reference after removing --reviewer"},{"path":"docs/mcp-reference.md","reason":"regenerated MCP reference after removing the review_code reviewers input"},{"path":"docs/adr/0075-retire-single-pass-code-review.md","reason":"correct ADR wording that still claimed the old signature was preserved unchanged"},{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","reason":"record the intentional pre-1.0 breaking contract change"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_review_ops_characterization.py","reason":"keep the review_result reviewers output pinned while removing the input"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_cli_help_writing_guidelines_jerboa.py","reason":"refresh the help-writing oracle after review-code lost --reviewer"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_advanced_cli_parsers.py","reason":"prove the parser rejects the removed --reviewer flag"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_code_review_gate_session.py","reason":"prove the CLI rejects and no longer forwards caller-selected reviewers"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_code_review_provenance_heldout_2d1c.py","reason":"prove the library surface rejects reviewers= while preserving provenance guarantees"},{"path":"tests/unit/mcp_library_parity_manifest.json","reason":"refresh the MCP/library parity baseline for the removed review_code input"},{"path":"tests/external/test_pydantic_ai_cutover_live.py","reason":"remove the retired reviewers input from live review_code call sites"},{"path":"tests/external/test_llm_trace.py","reason":"remove the retired reviewers input from trace coverage call sites"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86"],["relates_to","9199-1dc8-c0a4-4484"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86","parent_status_uuid":"bbee2d14-41f0-4aae-ab9c-ef87525b2dc8","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["janitor","api","breaking-change","rp18"],"ticket_id":"3c2f-01aa-7ea1-409b","ticket_type":"story","title":"Remove caller-selected reviewer inputs from code review contracts","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["8b34537f-a3db-47a1-96d7-a5781326828a","0a80a2db-00c8-41b0-a3a5-92c4aa608b1d","a71c3871-a50f-4070-aa73-545c6753128b","f00cbab9-19c9-4fa8-920e-d2c590279866","43ee9b99-e827-4ce3-8ee4-0b8b36c33fa8","eabdf1bc-3c1a-410d-8312-0e198326d643","44e919cc-1eba-4a8d-9312-7772b67bd6e5","b92d79f2-b666-4b03-b8b8-974da9d17acc","4ad217ff-abc3-4225-9f14-27fa70082f80","4d88ee0a-328e-4176-a16f